      "object 32": {
        "ID": 32,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "160.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "1. Click the button: 1, 2, 3 … each bang adds the step, 1, to the count. The first bang sends the start value plus the step, so a counter starting at 0 sends 1 first. Click 20: the count jumps to 20 and is sent, and the next bang gives 21.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 33": {
        "ID": 33,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "310.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. The right inlet sets the step. Click 3 and bang: the count goes up by 3. Click -1: it counts down. Click reset: back to the start value, without sending; the next bang sends the start value plus the step.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 34": {
        "ID": 34,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "460.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. Counting in a range. Click the lower button a few times. % 4 wraps the count: 1 2 3 0 1 … and pong 0 3 folds it back from the limits: 1 2 3 2 1 0 1 …, up and down.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 35": {
        "ID": 35,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "590.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. A step sequencer. Turn on the toggle: metro bangs the counter every 150 ms, % 4 turns the count into the steps 0 to 3, and sel sends each step to its own note, through mtof into a sine on the master bus. The toggle also opens its level.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 36": {
        "ID": 36,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "740.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "5. The carry. sel's first outlet fires each time the steps wrap round to 0, once a bar, and bangs a second counter that counts the bars: what Max's carry outlet does.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
